  ⚠ Remaining incompatibilities noted by connector LLM:
    - minimalmodbus has no TCP/IP Modbus client (no ModbusTcpClient equivalent); it only supports serial (RTU/ASCII) 
communication via pyserial, so host/port-based connection cannot be represented.
    - No `.connect()` method exists on minimalmodbus.Instrument — serial port opening happens implicitly at construction time 
with a device path, not a host/port pair.
    - minimalmodbus's `read_registers`/`read_register` methods return raw lists/values directly and raise exceptions on error,
rather than returning a response object with `.isError()` and `.registers` attributes as used in `read_measurement()` — this 
changes the response-handling API shape used downstream, which is itself a structural (not just wrapper-fixable at the 
client-construction level) mismatch given the whole call site pattern in read_measurement().
    - The `unit` parameter (multi-device addressing over one TCP connection) doesn't map cleanly onto minimalmodbus, which 
binds a single slave address at Instrument construction time per serial port; supporting multiple units per host would require
re-architecting the connection/instantiation strategy entirely.

