TelemetryBridge.publish_reading/publish_batch methods (and their callers) have no async execution context, so no wrapper can 
transparently bridge sync call sites to the async API without changing the public sync interface and its callers.
    - paho-mqtt's publish() return value exposes a synchronous `.rc` attribute used directly (`getattr(info, 'rc', 0)`); 
aiomqtt's publish() returns None (or raises) and provides no equivalent synchronous status object, so the rc-based result 
contract cannot be preserved without altering the client's dependency-injection contract used throughout the class.
    - The client_id constructor keyword and persistent client object semantics (single Client instance reused for many 
publishes across the object's lifetime) do not map onto aiomqtt's per-context-manager-session usage model.
