  ⚠ Remaining incompatibilities noted by connector LLM:
    - minimalmodbus provides no TCP/IP client abstraction (ModbusTcpClient equivalent); it only supports serial-line 
(RTU/ASCII) communication via a serial port device path, so host/port-based instantiation and client.connect() have no 
counterpart.
    - pymodbus read/write calls (read_holding_registers, write_register) return response objects with an isError() method and 
a .registers list; minimalmodbus's corresponding calls (read_register/read_registers, write_register) return plain ints/lists 
directly and signal errors via exceptions (e.g. minimalmodbus.NoResponseError, IllegalRequestError) rather than a 
boolean-checkable response object -- this error-model mismatch could be bridged with wrapper glue, but only if the underlying 
transport (serial vs TCP) were compatible in the first place.
    - The 'unit=' keyword argument (slave/unit id per call) used by pymodbus does not map cleanly onto minimalmodbus's model, 
where the slave address is bound to the Instrument instance at construction time, not passed per read/write call -- this is a 
structural API design difference, not merely a rename.
