ModbusTcpClient(host, port=...) has no counterpart in minimalmodbus -- this is a structural transport-layer mismatch, not 
something a wrapper can bridge without a serial device present.
    - pymodbus read/write calls return response objects exposing .isError() and .registers; minimalmodbus's 
read_register/read_registers/write_register return raw values directly and signal errors via exceptions instead of a response 
object -- this changes the error-handling and data-access model throughout ModbusIO, requiring rewriting call sites' control 
flow rather than a drop-in wrapper for a single call.
    - The 'unit' parameter passed per-call to pymodbus's read/write methods (Modbus slave/unit id) is not a per-call parameter
in minimalmodbus; slave address is fixed on the minimalmodbus.Instrument object at construction, requiring a different 
architecture (e.g., one Instrument per slave) rather than a single client used with variable unit ids.

