there is no sync equivalent API.
    - MqttSink.publish() is a synchronous method expected to return an int rc immediately; aiomqtt.Client.publish() is a 
coroutine, so any wrapper must either force a nested event loop per call (fragile, breaks if already inside an event loop, 
degrades performance) or change the public API to async, which is a structural change to callers, not something wrapper glue 
can transparently fix.
    - aiomqtt has no concept of a standalone MQTTMessageInfo return value with an `.rc` attribute; aiomqtt.publish() simply 
returns None on success or raises on failure, so the getattr(info, 'rc', 0) pattern has no faithful equivalent and any 
synthesized 'rc' would be fabricated, not a real broker acknowledgement code.

